config LOG
	bool "log: loggers, log sinks, and printf-style call sites"
	default y
	select STATUS
	select IO
	select FMT
	select TIME
	help
	  Logging for applications: a logger with a level, a tag, and a clock;
	  the el_log_sink interface that decides where records go; a sink
	  that writes text lines to an el_writer, and one that keeps records
	  in caller-provided memory; and the contract test suite for sinks.
	  Elemental's own modules never log.

config LOG_MESSAGE_MAX
	int "Longest message el_log_printf() formats, in bytes"
	default 128
	range 16 1024
	depends on LOG
	help
	  el_log_printf() and the EL_LOG_* macros format a message into this
	  many bytes on their own stack before the sink sees it, and cut a
	  longer one. Lower it for threads with small stacks; raise it for an
	  application that logs long lines. It changes how long a message
	  may be and how much stack a log call uses, never a type or a
	  signature. A message given to el_log_write() directly is not
	  limited by it.
